Day 43: Stay Close to Jesus | Spy Wednesday (Holy Week Devotional)

📌 YouTube Description
A friend turns away.
A disciple steps into the shadows.
A heart that once walked with Jesus chooses another road.

Welcome to Day 43 of our Holy Week journey.
Today is Spy Wednesday, the solemn day when Judas goes to the chief priests and begins the path of betrayal. This moment in Scripture is not meant to make you point fingers — it is meant to help you look honestly at your own heart, at the places where fear, fatigue, or discouragement tempt you to step back from Jesus.

This spoken‑word devotional invites you to remain close to Christ even when the path grows dark. In the midst of betrayal, Jesus remains steady, faithful, and present. He does not withdraw His love. He simply invites you — gently, honestly — to stay near.

In today’s reflection, you’ll hear:

Why Spy Wednesday reveals the contrast between betrayal and fidelity

How Jesus remains faithful even when others turn away

Why Holy Week invites you to stay close to Christ, one step at a time

A prayer for fidelity, devotion, and steady love

A simple daily activity: whispering, “Jesus, I choose to stay close.”

